# Changelog (engine/v1/)

## Tube loops gated on the centerline direction
**What:** A loop on a tube now engages only when its axis lies within 45° of the tube's centerline tangent nearest the player. Non-tube loop surfaces engage on any axis, as before. Only engagement is gated; a running loop is not released on a mismatch.
- `buildTube` returns its centerline: node centers plus connector ring points.
- `computeWorldCenterline` stores it in world space as `mesh.centerline` on the invisible, void and normal `BuildObject` paths (`null` for non-tubes).
- `sceneGraph.tubeCenterlines` maps a surface id to its centerline lines, gathered from terrain, void terrain and obstacle parts.
- `alongTube` is the last engage condition in `trackLoop`.

**Where:** [builder/NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js) (`buildTube`, `computeWorldCenterline`, `BuildObject`), [builder/NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js) (`tubeCenterlines`), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js) (`alongTube`, `trackLoop`).

## Small-loop roll exception limited to tube walls
**What:** `frame.onSmallLoop` now also requires `alongTube` for the slope's tilt axis (`cross(world up, alignedUp)`). A tube's walls, which tilt around its centerline, still don't roll. A bend along the tube's length rolls like a regular slope. Non-tube small-loop surfaces are unchanged.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js) (`detectSituation`).

## Void wall linings wound to face the cavity
**What:** Void wall linings now face into the cavity. Each void face carries `flipWinding` (`cavitySign < 0`), and `buildHostLining` pushes that face's lining triples as (a, c, b) when it is set.

**Where:** [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js) (`buildVoidFaces`, `buildHostLining`).

## Backface culling skips water and planes
**What:** `setFaceCulling(gl, cull)` turns on `CULL_FACE` only when `cull` is true and `CONFIG.Performance.BackfaceCulling` is on. It replaces the frame-start toggle in `drawScene`. Culling is set per mesh in `drawMeshList`, and is off for `primitive === "plane"` and for `options.cull === false`. `drawWaterPass` passes `cull: false`. The scatter instance, scatter decal and mesh decal passes also skip planes. Scatter instance results now carry `primitive`.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`setFaceCulling`, `drawMeshList`, `drawWaterPass`, `drawDecalPass`, `drawScatterDecalPass`, `buildScatterInstanceBuffers`, `drawScene`).

## trackLoop reads contactGrace
**What:** `contactGrace` is added to the `playerState` destructure in `trackLoop`, which fixes a ReferenceError on the first airborne frame.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js) (`trackLoop`).

## Trigger overlay split at the water line
**What:** The main mesh program has a `v_worldY` varying and a `u_waterClip` uniform (x = water level in world units, y = side kept: +1 above, −1 below, 0 keeps all). Clipped fragments get alpha 0 and are discarded. `drawMeshList` sets `u_waterClip` on every non-triplanar call (default `keepWholeMesh`). `drawTriggerOverlay` replaces PASS C. With water, `drawTranslucentPass` draws the far-side trigger half before the water and the near-side half after it. Without water, triggers draw whole before the translucents.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`createProgram`, `drawMeshList`, `drawTriggerOverlay`, `drawTranslucentPass`, `drawScene`).

## Triggers unculled and anchored at their authored base
**What:** `drawTriggerOverlay` passes `cull: false`. `buildTriggerMesh` centres the box at `start.y + triggerHeight * 0.5`, so the drawn and detected box spans `start.y` to `world.height`.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`drawTriggerOverlay`), [builder/NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js) (`buildTriggerMesh`).

## Toon and comic filters
**What:** `CONFIG.Rendering.Filters` is `{ ToonLines, Comic }` (replaces `Outlines`); both currently `true`. New exported `FILTER_TUNING` outside `API_CONFIG`: `Lines { Color, Width, Threshold }` and `Comic { LightDirection, Bands, ShadowFloor, ColorLevels, Halftone { CellSize, Strength } }`.
- `comicLightGLSL` in `createFoggedTextureFragmentShader` multiplies every surface program's color by a light band. The band comes from the screen-space face normal (turned toward the camera) and `FILTER_TUNING.Comic.LightDirection`, and is gated by a new `u_comic` uniform set in `configureTexturedMeshPass` from `passState.comic`.
- When either filter is on, `drawScene` draws into `renderer.sceneTarget` (RGBA8 color + DEPTH_COMPONENT24 depth textures from `ensureSceneTarget`, resized with the canvas). `drawFilterPass` (PASS F, after the translucent pass, before the debug overlays) then draws it to the canvas through `createFilterProgram`:
  - posterize plus halftone dots on geometry, when Comic is on
  - ink lines where inverse view depth bends, faded by fog, when ToonLines is on
  - the scene depth is written through `gl_FragDepth` with `depthFunc(ALWAYS)`
- With both filters off, the scene draws straight to the canvas as before.

**Where:** [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`API_CONFIG.Rendering.Filters`, `FILTER_TUNING`), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`comicLightGLSL`, `createFoggedTextureFragmentShader`, `createFilterProgram`, `createTargetTexture`, `ensureSceneTarget`, `ensureFilterQuad`, `ensureLevelRenderer`, `configureTexturedMeshPass`, `drawFilterPass`, `drawScene`).

## Toon lines under scatter and water; softer comic
**What:**
- **Ink pass:** ToonLines moved to `drawInkPass` (PASS E2, after decals, before scatter). The pass blits scene depth into `sceneTarget.edgeDepth` through `edgeFramebuffer`, then alpha-blends ink from `createInkProgram` onto the scene color. It drops ink for pixels whose rebuilt world height is on the far side of the water from the camera (`u_waterClip`).
- **Filter pass:** `createFilterProgram` now does comic and presenting only, sharing `fullscreenVertexGLSL`. Comic skips the sky. Posterize blends by `Posterize.Strength`, and halftone dots form only below `Halftone.Below` brightness.
- **`FILTER_TUNING.Comic`:**
  - `ColorLevels` replaced by `Posterize { Levels, Strength }`
  - `Halftone` gains `Below`
  - `ShadowFloor` changes from 0.6 to 0.75

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`fullscreenVertexGLSL`, `createInkProgram`, `createFilterProgram`, `ensureInkQuad`, `ensureSceneTarget`, `ensureLevelRenderer`, `drawInkPass`, `drawFilterPass`, `drawScene`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`FILTER_TUNING`).

## Antialiased filter target
**What:**
- **Multisampled target:** when filtered, `sceneTarget.framebuffer` draws into multisampled renderbuffers (`colorSamples` RGBA8, `depthSamples` DEPTH_COMPONENT24) at `FILTER_TUNING.Samples` (4) samples.
- **Resolves:** `resolveSceneTarget` blits the scene into `resolveFramebuffer`, which holds the `color`/`depth` textures, in `drawFilterPass` (color and depth). It blits into `edgeFramebuffer` in `drawInkPass` (depth).
- **Cleanup removed:** the texture unbinds after both passes are gone.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`ensureSceneTarget`, `resolveSceneTarget`, `drawInkPass`, `drawFilterPass`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`FILTER_TUNING.Samples`).

## Near-side water clip shared through passState
**What:**
- `drawScene` computes `passState.nearWaterClip` once: `keepWholeMesh` without water, otherwise `{ level, side }` keeping the camera's side.
- `drawInkPass` reads it and no longer takes a `waterClip` parameter.
- `drawTranslucentPass` destructures `level`/`side` from it for the trigger overlay halves.
- Comments in the toon code were rewritten.
- `FILTER_TUNING.Comic.Posterize` and `.Halftone` are multi-line objects with one comment per field.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`drawScene`, `drawInkPass`, `drawTranslucentPass`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`FILTER_TUNING`).

## Dead camera payload fields removed
**What:**
- `level.camera.sensitivity` was removed from the schema. Mouse sensitivity is `CONFIG.Camera.Sensitivity`.
- `level.camera.levelOpening.endPosition` was removed from the schema and from normalization. `startPosition` stays.
- The fields were also removed from the engine level template and from testGame's `levels.json` (2 stages) and `lvl2.json`.

**Where:** [core/canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json) (`level.camera`), [core/normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js) (level camera normalization), [builder/templates/levels.json](engine/v1/builder/templates/levels.json), [testGame/levels/levels.json](engine/v1/testGame/levels/levels.json), [testGame/levels/lvl2.json](engine/v1/testGame/levels/lvl2.json).

## LSM field-test one-line fixes
**What:**
- `flatDecalOrder` is now `[0, 2, 1, 1, 2, 3]`, so flat decal quads face outward from their host face.
- `handleLookInput` no longer consumes `pointerdown` while the pointer is already locked. The click falls through to `USER_INPUT`.
- `PlayAudio` captures its own id per call, and its `finalize` removes that id from the channel's active list.
- `BroadphaseCollectCandidates` skips terrain and obstacles whose `detailedBounds` is `null`.
- `CreateDetailedBoundsFromParts` returns `null` for `collisionShape: "none"`.
- `RayAABBDetailedBoundsIntersect` no longer has a null-bounds early return.
- StartupGuide's config paths now read `Debug.Skip`.

**Where:** [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`flatDecalOrder`), [camera/Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js) (`handleLookInput`), [handlers/Sound.js](engine/v1/handlers/Sound.js) (`PlayAudio`), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js) (`BroadphaseCollectCandidates`), [builder/NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js) (`CreateDetailedBoundsFromParts`), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js) (`RayAABBDetailedBoundsIntersect`), [docs/guides/StartupGuide.md](engine/v1/docs/guides/StartupGuide.md).

## Shaders and primitives split into their own modules
**What:**
- All WebGL shader code moved from `Render.js` to `handlers/utilities/Shaders.js`: shader compile/link helpers, the shared GLSL chunks, and the ten program builders.
- The program builders are exported as `CreateProgram`, `CreateEntityTriplanarProgram`, `CreateLineProgram`, `CreateScatterProgram`, `CreateDecalProgram`, `CreateScatterDecalProgram`, `CreateSkyProgram`, `CreateBlendProgram`, `CreateInkProgram` and `CreateFilterProgram`, and `Render.js` imports them. The CPU-side decal code stays in `Render.js`.
- All primitive shape construction moved from `NewObject.js` to `builder/NewPrimitive.js`: the complexity resolvers, the ring/fan/sector helpers, every `build<Shape>` function and its tube helpers, and `BuildGeometry`.
- `BuildGeometry` is exported only from `NewPrimitive.js`. `NewObject.js` and `NewScatter.js` import it from there. `NewPrimitive.js` imports `TransformPointByMatrix` from `NewObject.js`.
- UV generation, bounds, `TransformPointByMatrix` and `computeWorldCenterline` stay in `NewObject.js`.
- No behavior change.

**Where:** [handlers/utilities/Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [builder/NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js), [builder/NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [builder/NewScatter.js](engine/v1/builder/NewScatter.js).

## Shader builders exported as one default object
**What:**
- The `Create` prefix was dropped from the `Shaders.js` program builders. They are now `Program`, `EntityTriplanarProgram`, `LineProgram`, `ScatterProgram`, `DecalProgram`, `ScatterDecalProgram`, `SkyProgram`, `BlendProgram`, `InkProgram` and `FilterProgram`.
- They are exported as one default object instead of named exports. This replaces the `Create*` names listed in "Shaders and primitives split into their own modules".
- `Render.js` imports the object as `CreateShader` and calls `CreateShader.<Name>(gl)`.

**Where:** [handlers/utilities/Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js).

## Pyramid centered; cylinder-cap decals resolve Flat
**What:**
- `buildPyramid` is centered on its local origin. The base sits at `y = -size.y / 2` and the apex at `y = +size.y / 2`. Before, the base was at `0` and the apex at `size.y`.
- `ResolveDecalShapeCode` compares its capitalised key against `"Cylinder"`, so decals on cylinder `top`/`bottom` caps resolve `DECAL_SHAPE_CODES.Flat`. Before, they resolved `Cylinder`. The renderer and the Simulator exporter both pick this up.

**Where:** [builder/NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js) (`buildPyramid`), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`ResolveDecalShapeCode`).

## Curved primitives lie flat when rotated 90°
**What:**
- `appendRadialVertices` takes an optional `angleOffset` (default `0`).
- `buildCylinder` (side quads and both cap rings), `buildCapsule` (every ring) and `appendTubeRing` (every tube cross-section, outer and inner) turn their rings by `Math.PI / segments`.
- `appendTubeConnectorFaceGroups` adds the same `Math.PI / segments` to each sector's `midAngle`, so the radial face-group normals stay centred on their sectors.
- `buildSphere` adds `Math.PI / slices` to `theta`. Its uvs are unchanged.
- `resolveSphereResolution` stacks are `7`/`13`/`19` (low/medium/high), up from `6`/`12`/`18`.
- Cone and torus are unchanged.

**Where:** [builder/NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js) (`appendRadialVertices`, `resolveSphereResolution`, `buildCylinder`, `buildSphere`, `buildCapsule`, `appendTubeRing`, `appendTubeConnectorFaceGroups`).

## Void carve uses a triangle grid
**What:**
- `math/Collision.js`:
  - `insideRayCrosses(point, triangle)` is the per-triangle ray test, split out of `PointInsideMesh`. `PointInsideMesh` now calls it, with the same signature and result.
  - New exports:
    - `BuildTriangleGrid(triangles, triangleAabbs)` splits a mesh's bounds into equal cells, each listing the triangles that touch it.
    - `TriangleGridCandidates(grid, aabb)` returns the triangle indices in the cells a box touches, ascending. It returns every index when the box spans more cells than there are triangles.
    - `PointInsideTriangleGrid(point, grid)` gives the same answer as `PointInsideMesh`, testing only triangles in the cells the ray passes through.
- `NewVoid.js`:
  - `buildCuttingSolid` builds a `grid` for every host and void solid. `candidateIndices` and the `buildCandidates` flag are removed.
  - `resolveCavitySign`, `buildVoidFaces` and `pieceInsideSolid` take a solid and use `PointInsideTriangleGrid`.
  - `collectCrossingPlanes` and `carveTriangleByVoid` take their candidates from `TriangleGridCandidates`.
  - `drainPairings` and `buildObstacleVoidWalls` push items one at a time instead of spreading an array into `push`.
  - The "Void classification complete" log now ends with `ms=`.
- `config.js`: new export `CARVE_GRID_TRIANGLES_PER_CELL = 2`, outside `API_CONFIG`.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js) (`insideRayCrosses`, `PointInsideMesh`, `BuildTriangleGrid`, `TriangleGridCandidates`, `PointInsideTriangleGrid`), [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js) (`buildCuttingSolid`, `resolveCavitySign`, `buildVoidFaces`, `pieceInsideSolid`, `collectCrossingPlanes`, `carveTriangleByVoid`, `drainPairings`, `buildObstacleVoidWalls`, `BuildVoidWalls`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`CARVE_GRID_TRIANGLES_PER_CELL`).

## Void host detection uses the triangle grids; spread pushes replaced
**What:**
- `MeshesIntersect(solidA, solidB)` takes cutting solids instead of `(triangles, aabb)` pairs.
  - Containment uses `PointInsideTriangleGrid` against the other solid's grid.
  - `edgesCrossMesh(triangles, targetGrid)` tests each edge only against `TriangleGridCandidates` for the edge's bounding box.
  - The opening `AabbOverlap` reject is removed.
- `collectRelationHosts(voidSolid, hosts)` builds a host's cutting solid on that host's first strict AABB overlap with a void. Hosts start as `{ mesh, recordId, solid: null }` and no longer carry `triangles`.
- Terrain and obstacle voids call `buildVoidFaces` only when they have at least one related host.
- Four array spreads into `push` are now per-item loop pushes:
  - obstacle triangle soups
  - void-wall lining triangles
  - openFaces grouped by object id
  - built terrain meshes

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js) (`edgesCrossMesh`, `MeshesIntersect`), [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js) (`collectRelationHosts`, `buildTerrainVoidWalls`, `buildObstacleVoidWalls`), [builder/NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js), [builder/NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [builder/NewTerrain.js](engine/v1/builder/NewTerrain.js) (`BuildTerrain`).

## Frustum culling and the entity render gate
**What:**
- `math/Matrix.js`: new `FrustumPlanes(matrix)` returns the six inward-facing view walls of a projection × view matrix, each as `[x, y, z, offset]`.
- `math/Collision.js`: new `AabbOutsideFrustum(planes, aabb, padding = 0)` returns true when the box, optionally padded, sits fully behind any one wall.
- `core/config.js`: new `PERFORMANCE_SCALING.Culling.EntityPadding = new Unit(2, "cnu")`.
- `handlers/Render.js`:
  - `drawScene` builds the frustum from `MultiplyMatrix4(projection, view)`, stores it on `passState.frustum`, and calls `hideOffscreen` before `collectRenderableMeshes`.
  - New `hideOffscreen` sets `performance.rendering = false` for terrain meshes, obstacle records and entities that are fully off screen. Entities are tested with `entityRenderBounds` (all part boxes merged, or the single mesh's box), padded by `EntityPadding`.
  - `collectRenderableMeshes` and the entity loop in `drawDecalPass` skip entities whose `performance.rendering` is false.
  - `drawVoidWalls` draws only the void-wall meshes that are on screen.

**Where:** [math/Matrix.js](engine/v1/math/Matrix.js) (`FrustumPlanes`), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js) (`AabbOutsideFrustum`), [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`PERFORMANCE_SCALING.Culling`), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`drawScene`, `entityRenderBounds`, `hideOffscreen`, `collectRenderableMeshes`, `drawDecalPass`, `drawVoidWalls`).

## Scatter drawn per visible ground square
**What:**
- **`core/config.js`:** `PERFORMANCE_SCALING.Culling` gains `ScatterCellSize = new Unit(20, "cnu")`.
- **`handlers/Render.js`:**
  - `buildInstancedVao` takes an optional `instanceOffset` (bytes, default `0`), added to every instance attribute's offset.
  - New `groupInstancesIntoCells(instanceData, instanceCount, instanceReach)`:
    - Copies a batch's instances into a new `Float32Array`, grouped by XZ ground square. Order is kept within each square.
    - Returns one `{ start, count, aabb }` per square. The box grows each instance's position by the shape's reach times its matrix's scaling.
  - `buildScatterInstanceBuffers`:
    - Measures each batch's `instanceReach` from its shared primitive geometry.
    - Uploads the grouped data and builds one VAO per square (`cell.vao`). Each decal draw gets matching `cellVaos`.
    - Batch results carry `cells` instead of `vao`.
    - The ready log reports the cell count and cell size.
  - New `scatterCellVisible(cell, passState)`: a square passes if its box is within `passState.cullRadius` of `passState.cameraPosition` and not fully outside `passState.frustum`.
  - The scatter pass and `drawScatterDecalPass` issue one instanced draw per visible square.
  - `passState` gains `cameraPosition`.
  - `sceneGraph` scatter `instanceData` is not modified.

**Where:** [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`PERFORMANCE_SCALING.Culling`), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`buildInstancedVao`, `groupInstancesIntoCells`, `buildScatterInstanceBuffers`, `scatterCellVisible`, `drawScatterDecalPass`, `drawScene`).

## Scatter dissolve always reaches full opacity
**What:**
- In `scatterCullGLSL`, each instance's `cullHash` is now scaled by `0.75`. The instance's quarter-wide dissolve (`clamp((fade - cullHash) * 4.0, 0, 1)`) now always finishes before `fade` reaches 1.
- The blade and scatter decal shaders both use this cull code, so both get the fix.

**Where:** [handlers/utilities/Shaders.js](engine/v1/handlers/utilities/Shaders.js) (`scatterCullGLSL`).

## Loop counts steady frames as exact game steps
**What:**
- **`core/config.js`:** new exported `FRAME_SNAP = { Frames: 4, WindowMs: 1 }`, outside `PERFORMANCE_SCALING`.
- **`handlers/game/Level.js`:**
  - `levelLoop` gains `recentFrames`, which is reset in `StartLevelLoop`.
  - Each unpaused frame averages the last `FRAME_SNAP.Frames` frame times. If the average is within `FRAME_SNAP.WindowMs` of a whole number of fixed steps, the accumulator gains exactly that many steps. Otherwise it gains the real frame time.
  - TEMP: `pacingProbe` logs an error for any second with 3 or more frames that ran 2+ steps. It reports frames, drawn, catch-ups, longest gap and longest work. It is to be removed once the fix is verified.

**Where:** [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js) (`FRAME_SNAP`), [handlers/game/Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js) (`levelLoop`, `pacingProbe`, `StartLevelLoop`).

## Frame-step values inlined; pacing probe removed
**What:**
- **`core/config.js`:** `FRAME_SNAP` and its export are removed.
- **`handlers/game/Level.js`:**
  - The loop's frame-step check now uses inline values: a 4-frame average and a 1 ms window.
  - The TEMP `pacingProbe` and its per-second error log are removed.

**Where:** [core/config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [handlers/game/Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js) (`StartLevelLoop`).

## Shared triangle, bounds and vertex-read helpers moved into math/
**What:**
- **`math/Collision.js`:**
  - New exports `TriangleNormal(a, b, c)` (zero vector when degenerate), `TriangleArea(a, b, c)` and `TriangleCentroid(a, b, c)`. They replace the unused private `triangleNormal`.
  - New BOUNDS FROM AABB section exports `SphereFromAabb(aabb, inscribed)`, `CapsuleFromAabb(aabb)` and `ObbFromAabb(aabb)`.
  - `BuildTriangleGrid`'s area sum uses `TriangleArea`.
- **`math/Matrix.js`:** `TransformPointByMatrix` moved here from `builder/NewObject.js`, which no longer exports it.
- **`math/Vector3.js`:** new `ArrayToVector3(array, index)` reads vertex `index` out of a flat xyz array.
- **Builders now call the shared helpers instead of local copies:**
  - `NewObject.js`: drops `computeSphereFromMesh`, `computeCapsuleFromMesh` and `getVertexVector`.
  - `NewEntity.js`: drops `computeCapsuleFromAabb`, `computeSphereFromAabb` (now `SphereFromAabb(…, true)`) and `computeObbFromAabb`. `transformOffset` now calls `rotateWithTrig`.
  - `NewObstacle.js`: drops `createEnvelopeObb`, `createEnvelopeSphere` and `createEnvelopeCapsule`.
  - `NewVoid.js`: drops `windingNormal`, `computeTriangleNormal` and `triangleArea`.
  - `NewLevel.js`: `boxFacets` now takes an obb object. Aabb bounds go through `ObbFromAabb`, and the surface-chunk centroid uses `TriangleCentroid`.
  - `NewPrimitive.js`: the pyramid face normal and the tube ring vertex reads use the shared helpers.
- **Handlers:** `Render.js` and `Simulator.js` import `TransformPointByMatrix` from `math/Matrix.js` and read vertices with `ArrayToVector3`. Render's degenerate-facet check is `TriangleArea(...) < 5e-15`. Simulator's glTF `triangleNormal` wraps `TriangleNormal`.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [math/Matrix.js](engine/v1/math/Matrix.js), [math/Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js), [builder/NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [builder/NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js), [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js), [builder/NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [builder/NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [handlers/game/Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js).

## Sphere-collision obstacles get a sphere envelope
**What:**
- `CreateDetailedBoundsFromParts`: a `collisionShape: "sphere"` obstacle now gets `SphereFromAabb(bounds, false)`. It used to get a capsule.

**Where:** [builder/NewObstacle.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObstacle.js) (`CreateDetailedBoundsFromParts`).

## Shared AABB center and half-size helpers
**What:**
- **`math/Collision.js`:** new exports `AabbCenter(aabb)` and `AabbHalfExtents(aabb)`, which return plain vectors. The box contact functions and the three collider builders use them. The `UnitVector3` fields are built with `.clone().set(...)`.
- **`physics/Collision.js`:**
  - The private `getAabbCenter` and `getHalfExtents` are removed.
  - `buildEntityAabbAtPosition` is removed. The trigger overlap test now uses `entity.collision.aabb` directly.
  - `checkSweptAabbPair` drops its `position` parameter.
- **Other callers use the shared helpers:**
  - `physics/Correction.js`: `PoseAnchor`.
  - `camera/Modes.js`: `AimPoint`.
  - `builder/NewObject.js`: `computeObbFromMesh`.
  - `builder/NewEntity.js`: the aabb case of `computeScaledBounds`.
- **Vertex reads:** `handlers/Render.js` (scatter `instanceReach`) and `handlers/game/Simulator.js` (the decal nearest-facet loop) now read vertices with `ArrayToVector3`.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [physics/Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [camera/Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [builder/NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [handlers/game/Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js).

## `ArrayToVector3` gains a `multiplied` flag; hand-written triple reads use it
**What:**
- **`math/Vector3.js`:** `ArrayToVector3(array, index, multiplied)`. With `multiplied`, `index` is a vertex in a flat xyz array (`index * 3`). Without it, the three values are read from `index` directly.
- **Existing vertex reads** now pass `true`: `Render.js`, `NewPrimitive.js`, `NewObject.js`, `NewVoid.js`, `Simulator.js`.
- **Hand-written triples replaced** with `ArrayToVector3`, or `Vector3ToArray(ArrayToVector3(...))` where an array is needed:
  - `Render.js`: `DecalSurfaceUv` placement columns, `createObbLineVertices` axes.
  - `NewObject.js`: `computeObbFromMesh` model-matrix axes.
  - `NewPrimitive.js`: `makeTubeNode` frame columns.
  - `Simulator.js`: `buildMeshVertices` index triple, `buildDecalVertices` `faceAxis` and `decalCenter`.
  - `math/Collision.js`: `projectObbRadiusOntoAxis`.
  - `NewVoid.js`: `groupCoplanarPieces` triples, `buildVoidFaces` and `carveHostGeometry` index triples, `buildVoidMesh` face-group `vertexIndices`.
- **Fix:** `NewVoid.js` `buildVoidMesh` (both branches) now spreads the lining position into `newPositions`. It was pushing a nested array.

**Where:** [math/Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js), [builder/NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js), [builder/NewPrimitive.js](engine/v1/builder/NewPrimitive.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [handlers/game/Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js).

## Inside-box and AABB-vs-AABB contacts simplified; collision bug fixes
**What:**
- **`math/Vector3.js`:** new `MinAxisVector3`, the index of a vector's smallest component.
- **`math/Collision.js`:**
  - `resolveInsideAabbContact` and `resolveInsideObbContact` are merged into `resolveInsideBoxContact`.
  - New module constant `worldBoxAxes`, used by `AabbObbContact`, `aabbTriangleSetContact` and `ObbFromAabb`.
  - New `worldBoxFaces` and `obbFaces`: each box axis's negative and positive face normals, used by `resolveInsideBoxContact` and `AabbAabbContact`.
  - `chooseDeepestContact` is exported as `ChooseDeepestContact`.
- **AABB-vs-AABB contact:** `aabbAabbContact` moves from physics/Collision.js to math/Collision.js as the exported `AabbAabbContact`. The duplicate `chooseDeepestContact` in physics/ is removed; `iterateCompoundSpheres` uses the shared one.
- **`handlers/Render.js`:** `createObbLineVertices` now scales each OBB axis by its own half-extent. It multiplied a vector of axis vectors, which gave the debug wireframe NaN corners.
- **Fixes to the uncommitted math/Collision.js edits:**
  - `projectObbRadiusOntoAxis` returned NaN.
  - `ClosestPointOnTriangle` lost `ac` on the a→c edge and set an undeclared `w` for interior points.
  - `TriangleAabb` read `triangle.x`.
- **`rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md` §5.2:** a declared function that spans lines uses `function`; only one-line functions may be `const`. Inline callbacks are exempt.

**Where:** [math/Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md).

## `BestMatchOf` adopted; soup contacts share `deepestContactInBox`; scatter-decal crash fix
**What:**
- **`math/Utilities.js`:** `BestMatchOf(array, condition, currentBest, storage)`, the author's version, is now exported.
- **`BestMatchOf` call sites:**
  - `math/Collision.js`: the `aabbTriangleSetContact` facing-triangle pick.
  - `builder/NewEntity.js`: the face-to-world-axis alignment pick.
- **`math/Collision.js`:** new `deepestContactInBox(triangles, box, contactWith)`. `SphereTriangleSoupContact`, `CapsuleTriangleSoupContact`, `SphereVoidWallContact` and `CapsuleVoidWallContact` are now one-line calls to it.
- **`handlers/Render.js`:** `drawScatterDecalPass` read `scatterDecalShader.uniform` instead of `.uniforms`, so the first uniform set threw at level start.

**Where:** [math/Utilities.js](engine/v1/math/Utilities.js), [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js), [builder/NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [handlers/Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js).

## Void-carved hosts no longer vanish
**What:**
- **Fixes to the uncommitted `carveHostGeometry` refactor:**
  - `groupStart` is captured before each face-texture group's triangle loop again. It was read after the loop, so every group had 0 indices and carved hosts drew nothing.
  - A blended carve vertex takes its index from `posSliced` before the push. It read the unsliced `positions`, so every new vertex shared one index.
- **`drainCarveQueue`:** the "after" triangle and vertex totals read `hostMesh.geometry` after the carve again, not arrays destructured before it.

**Where:** [builder/NewVoid.js](engine/v1/builder/NewVoid.js).

## `AzimuthTurnVector3` gives no turn for vertical vectors
**What:**
- **`math/Vector3.js`:** `AzimuthTurnVector3` returns a zero turn when either vector has no horizontal component (`hypot(x, z) <= EPSILON`).

**Where:** [math/Vector3.js](engine/v1/math/Vector3.js).

## chaseCam no longer freezes the input basis after a loop
**What:**
- **`prepareChase`:** always returns the live `armBasis`. On `leftLoop` it still sets `returning = true`, but no longer freezes a behind-the-facing basis.
- **`chaseRuntime.frozenBasis`:** removed, along with its resets in `initializeChase` and on look input.

**Where:** [camera/Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js).

## A carried lock outside a loop needs a throttling A/D
**What:**
- **`UpdateMovement`:** outside a loop, a carried lock now drops unless A/D is held and throttling it (`input.right !== 0 && lockThrottle > 0`). Before, it only dropped on a key change.

**Where:** [player/Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js).

## chaseCam's post-loop return trails the exit facing
**What:**
- **`chaseRuntime.exitFacing`:** new. `prepareChase` clones the target's facing into it on `leftLoop`.
- **`updateChase`:** trails `exitFacing` while `returning`, and the live facing otherwise.

**Where:** [camera/Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js).
